# The Envoy image's own build-context filter. BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore beside the
# Dockerfile in place of the context's root .dockerignore, and every build of this Dockerfile is a
# BuildKit one (docker/build-push-action in release-envoy-listener.yaml and ci-job-envoy-smoke.yaml,
# docker compose). It is the root .dockerignore with one change: of the envoy-infra module
# (packages/envoy/infra), this image builds /usr/local/bin/envoy-infra, so it lets in that module's
# module and workspace files and its Go sources but tests. The worker image, which copies
# packages/envoy whole, keeps the root file, which leaves the module out, so an envoy-infra change
# rebuilds this image and not that one. Change the two files together.
.git
.jj
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
*.log
# An operator's untracked environment files (.env, .env.local and the like, which .gitignore
# ignores anywhere), at the root and under every directory a COPY takes whole.
**/.env
**/.env.*
.vscode
.idea
**/docker-data
tmp
docs
# The documentation site is a root workspace, so every frozen Bun install needs its manifest
# (.github/scripts/check-bun-workspace-manifests.sh).
!docs/site/package.json
skills/AGENTS.md

# Every folder named out, which .gitignore ignores anywhere and no build reads from the context
# (the root .dockerignore says why).
**/out

# Envoy: test files and deploy tooling not needed in the image.
packages/envoy/**/*_test.go
packages/envoy/internal/integration/
packages/envoy/internal/smoke/
packages/envoy/deploy/
# The envoy-infra module: what `go build ./cmd/envoy-infra` reads and nothing else, its module and
# workspace files and its Go sources but tests (packages/envoy/**/*_test.go above). Each of its
# other files is left out by name - its guides, docs, scripts, test data and the held-port
# wrapper's Dockerfile - rather than the module left out and its Go sources taken back: a `!` line
# with a wildcard makes BuildKit walk every directory this file leaves out (.git, each
# node_modules) to look for a match, where it skips them while every `!` line is a plain path.
# A pull request that adds another file here fails check-image-trigger-paths.sh, since
# release-envoy-listener.yaml's push paths take only the files this lets in.
packages/envoy/infra/*.md
packages/envoy/infra/docs/
packages/envoy/infra/scripts/
packages/envoy/infra/**/testdata/
packages/envoy/infra/host/heldportwrapper/Dockerfile
packages/envoy/infra/host/heldportwrapper/Dockerfile.dockerignore

# Every package's changelog fragments, which no build reads.
packages/*/.changes/
